## Summary

The Open column in the Kanban board currently shows all open, unblocked tasks without distinguishing their planning readiness. This task adds a visual badge to each card in the Open column to indicate whether the task still needs a design/plan ("Needs Plan" badge) or already has an approved plan and is ready for implementation ("Ready" badge). This enables the lead to quickly identify which open tasks need planning agents vs which are ready for implementation agents.

## Technical Approach

Follow the existing badge pattern used by the review type badges (plan/code/help) in the Needs Review column. The approach is:

1. Create a utility function `getOpenStatus()` (similar to `getReviewType()`) that determines whether an open issue has a design or not
2. Add a new badge type to the IssueCard component that renders in the Open column
3. Add corresponding CSS styles following the existing badge patterns

The key design decision: use the `issue.design` field (already available in the Issue type and returned by the API) as the indicator. If `design` is truthy (non-empty string), the task is "Ready" for implementation. If `design` is falsy (undefined/empty/not present), the task "Needs Plan".

This approach is simple, requires no backend changes, and aligns with how the codebase already determines review types.

