## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **Tool entry with tool_input but no content (seq 5):** SessionDetailView checks \`!entry.content && entry.tool_input\` — renders tool_input as fallback. Assert \"npm test\" visible. Abort and return error if neither content nor tool_input is present (both undefined) — that entry renders with no content div, which is acceptable.
2. **Session with has_diff=false (sess-002):** Diff tab button has \`disabled\` attribute and \`title=\"No diff available\"\`. \`useSessionDiff\` receives \`enabled=false\` so no fetch occurs. Assert button is disabled.
3. **Diff endpoint 404:** \`getSessionDiff\` catches \`ApiError\` with status 404 and returns \`null\`. Component renders \"No diff available\" in \`diffEmpty\` class. Assert text visible.
4. **Diff endpoint 500:** \`getSessionDiff\` does NOT catch 500 errors — they propagate to \`diffError\` state. Component renders \"Failed to load diff: {message}\". Assert text visible.
5. **Transcript endpoint 500:** Same pattern as diff — error propagates to \`transcriptError\`. Component renders \"Failed to load transcript: {message}\".
6. **Empty transcript (zero entries):** Component checks \`!transcriptLoading && !transcriptError && entries.length === 0\` → renders \"No transcript entries\".
7. **Transcript loading:** Component checks \`transcriptLoading && entries.length === 0\` → renders \"Loading transcript...\". Only shows on first fetch (no cached entries). Use \`transcriptDelay\` option to trigger.
8. **Diff loading:** Component checks \`diffLoading\` → renders \"Loading diff...\". Use \`diffDelay\` option to trigger.
9. **No files_touched (sess-002):** The \`files_touched\` field is \`undefined\` — SessionDetailView checks \`session.files_touched && session.files_touched.length > 0\`, so the entire \`<details>\` section is not rendered.
10. **Inner tab switching:** Transcript and diff are mutually exclusive via \`innerTab\` React state — when one is visible the other is not rendered (conditional rendering with \`{innerTab === \"transcript\" && ...}\`). Switching tabs does NOT cause re-fetch of transcript (entries are cached in hook state) but DOES re-trigger diff fetch (new useEffect run).
11. **SSE connection:** Must call \`sse.sendConnected()\` after \`page.goto\` to simulate the server connected event. Without it, the SSE context may show a disconnected warning.

