## Summary

This task wires the task router (cjml5.6), concurrency tracker (cjml5.7), and expanded role constraints (cjml5.5) into the daemon supervisor loop. Currently, the daemon spawns agents with simple backend resolution (per-agent > project > global > default) and uses no role-based filtering, concurrency limits, or tool restrictions. After this integration, the daemon will:
1. Enforce per-role concurrency limits before spawning agents
2. Resolve backends through an extended chain (per-agent > per-role > project > global > default)
3. Apply tool allow/deny lists via a new ToolAwareBackend interface
4. Prepend read-only preamble for read-only roles
5. Use the task router's SelectBestTask in automode for roles with skill/path constraints

## Technical Approach

**Integration pattern**: Minimally invasive — add new fields and method calls at precise points in the existing superviseAgent loop and buildCommand method. All new behavior is gated on the presence of new config fields; when absent, the existing behavior is preserved exactly.

**Concurrency**: The ConcurrencyTracker's blocking Acquire() call is placed between branch setup (step 2) and spawn (step 3) in the supervise loop, using the shutdown channel for clean interruption. Release happens in a deferred function set immediately after successful Acquire, ensuring the slot is freed even on panics or early returns.

**Backend resolution**: Extended in buildCommand() to check per-role backend (from RoleConfig.Backend) between the per-agent and project-level checks. No new function needed — just one additional condition in the existing chain.

**Tool constraints**: A new optional ToolAwareBackend interface extends Backend with SetAllowedTools/SetDeniedTools methods. applyRoleConstraints() checks if the resolved backend implements this interface and applies the lists. Backends that don't implement the interface simply ignore tool constraints (backward compatible). The read-only preamble is prepended to the prompt, not injected via tool constraints, since it affects agent behavior broadly.

**Task routing in automode**: A new function wrapAutoModeWithRouter() creates AutoModeOptions.CustomTaskCheck and CustomPromptGen closures that use SelectBestTask from task_router.go instead of the generic Has*Tasks() functions. This is only enabled when the role has Skills, PathPatterns, or MaxPriority set. When none of these are set, the existing task checking functions are used unchanged.

