## Summary

Every `ConnectionPool.Get()` call executes a Ping RPC to the bd daemon before returning the connection to the caller. This doubles the RPC traffic per request and adds latency to every handler.

## Root Cause

`internal/webui/daemon/pool.go:125-131` — Get path calls `validateConnection(client)` at pool.go:322, which does `client.Ping()` — a full Unix socket round-trip.

Under the perf-sim's 4 RPS with multiple concurrent handlers, this adds ~50-100ms per request in Ping overhead alone, and doubles the Unix socket message count to the bd daemon.

## Fix

Replace Ping-on-borrow with lazy validation: use the connection without pinging and only validate (or discard+recreate) on RPC error. This halves per-request socket traffic.

```go
// Instead of:
func (p *Pool) Get() (*Client, error) {
    client := <-p.pool
    if err := validateConnection(client); err != nil {
        // reconnect...
    }
    return client, nil
}

// Use:
func (p *Pool) Get() (*Client, error) {
    client := <-p.pool
    return client, nil  // validate lazily on first RPC error
}
```

## Key Files
- internal/webui/daemon/pool.go:125-131 — Get with validateConnection
- internal/webui/daemon/pool.go:322-333 — validateConnection → Ping

