## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **Editing a comment that was deleted by someone else while in edit mode**: saveEdit calls editComment which returns 409 "cannot edit deleted comment". The handler shows the error message in the edit mode error area. The user must cancel the edit. The parent will update the comment's deleted_at via SSE, which will re-render CommentItem as a tombstone and exit edit mode (because the isEditing useEffect syncs on comment.deleted_at — if deleted_at becomes truthy while editing, force exit edit mode).

2. **Deleting a comment that was already deleted**: deleteComment returns success (idempotent per hfsf0.2 design). The handler calls onCommentDeleted. No error.

3. **Editing with empty text**: saveEdit trims text. If empty after trim, show error "Comment text cannot be empty" and stay in edit mode. Do NOT call the API.

4. **Editing with unchanged text**: saveEdit detects no change (trimmed text === comment.text.trim()) and exits edit mode without API call. Same as EditableDescription behavior.

5. **Reaction toggle while another toggle is in flight**: Use a local `isTogglingReaction` state (or a Set<string> of emoji being toggled) to disable the reaction chip button during the API call. This prevents double-toggling race conditions. If the API fails, show a brief error that auto-clears after 3 seconds.

6. **Comment with no author (empty string)**: Display "Unknown" as the author name, same as CommentsSection line 60. Edit/delete buttons are hidden (empty string !== "web-ui").

7. **Comment with edited_at but no deleted_at**: Show the "(edited)" badge. Normal view mode.

8. **Comment with both edited_at and deleted_at**: Show tombstone only. The "(edited)" badge is irrelevant for deleted comments.

9. **Reactions on a deleted comment**: Don't show reactions or action row for tombstone comments. Only show the tombstone text and timestamp.

10. **No reactions (empty array or undefined)**: Don't render the reaction strip at all. No empty state needed.

11. **currentUser is undefined**: Default to empty string. No edit/delete buttons shown (empty string won't match any author). Reaction toggle still works (author is set by the backend via reqActor, not the client).

12. **onReply is undefined**: Don't render the Reply button. The action row only shows edit/delete (if applicable).

13. **Long comment text in edit mode**: The textarea auto-resizes based on content (useEffect with scrollHeight), matching EditableDescription behavior. Minimum height is 80px.

14. **Force exit edit mode when comment.deleted_at changes**: Add a useEffect that watches comment.deleted_at. If it becomes truthy while isEditing is true, call cancelEdit() to force the user out of edit mode. This handles the case where an SSE event updates the comment to deleted while the user is editing.

