```

**Internal state:**

```typescript
const [focusedIndex, setFocusedIndex] = useState(0);
const containerRef = useRef<HTMLDivElement>(null);
const buttonRefs = useRef<(HTMLButtonElement | null)[]>([]);
```

**Effects:**

1. Click-outside handler (same pattern as PriorityDropdown lines 86-101): When `isOpen` is true, register a `mousedown` listener on document. If click target is outside `containerRef.current`, call `onClose()`. Cleanup removes listener.

2. Focus management: When `isOpen` transitions to true, focus the first emoji button via `requestAnimationFrame(() => buttonRefs.current[0]?.focus())`. Reset `focusedIndex` to 0.

3. Focus sync: When `focusedIndex` changes and `isOpen` is true, call `buttonRefs.current[focusedIndex]?.focus()`.

**Handlers:**

- `handleSelect(emoji: string)`: Call `onSelect(emoji)`, then call `onClose()`. The parent is responsible for the API call and error handling.

- `handleKeyDown(e: React.KeyboardEvent)`: Grid-aware keyboard navigation:
  - `ArrowRight`: Move to next emoji (wrap to start if at end)
  - `ArrowLeft`: Move to previous emoji (wrap to end if at start)
  - `ArrowDown`: Move down one row (+GRID_COLUMNS, clamp to last index)
  - `ArrowUp`: Move up one row (-GRID_COLUMNS, clamp to 0)
  - `Enter` / `Space`: Select the focused emoji via `handleSelect(EMOJI_OPTIONS[focusedIndex].emoji)`
  - `Escape`: Call `onClose()` with `e.stopPropagation()` (prevents parent handlers from firing, matching PriorityDropdown line 104-111)
  - `Tab`: Prevent default (trap focus inside popover)
  - All navigation keys call `e.preventDefault()`.

**Render:**

```tsx
export function ReactionPicker({
  isOpen,
  onSelect,
  onClose,
  className,
}: ReactionPickerProps): JSX.Element | null {
  // ... hooks ...

  if (!isOpen) return null;

  const rootClassName = [styles.reactionPicker, className]
    .filter(Boolean)
    .join(" ");

  return (
    <div ref={containerRef} className={rootClassName}>
      <div
        className={styles.menu}
        role="menu"
        aria-label="Add reaction"
        data-testid="reaction-picker-menu"
        onKeyDown={handleKeyDown}
      >
        {EMOJI_OPTIONS.map((option, index) => (
          <button
            key={option.emoji}
            ref={(el) => { buttonRefs.current[index] = el; }}
            type="button"
            className={styles.emojiButton}
            role="menuitem"
            aria-label={option.label}
            data-focused={index === focusedIndex || undefined}
            onClick={() => handleSelect(option.emoji)}
            data-testid={`reaction-picker-emoji-${option.emoji}`}
          >
            {option.emoji}
          </button>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  );
}
```

