## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **Session recovery on reload:** When the page reloads, useTerminalSessions fetches existing sessions from the backend. The useEffect maps them to tabs, restoring the previous tab state. The "talk-to-lead" session is always present (backend guarantee). Previously-created user sessions (e.g. "auth-redesign") appear if their tmux sessions are still running.

2. **Hook loading state:** While useTerminalSessions is loading, show a simple "Loading sessions..." placeholder instead of rendering empty tabs. Once loaded, initialize tabs from the session list.

3. **Hook error / API unavailable:** useTerminalSessions falls back to DEFAULT_SESSIONS containing just "talk-to-lead". TerminalView still works with a single tab.

4. **Max 8 tabs:** handleNewTabClick returns early and does not open the prompt when tabs.length >= 8.

5. **Duplicate session name:** SessionNamePrompt checks the typed name against existingNames. If it matches, show an inline error and disable submit. This prevents two tabs pointing at the same tmux session.

6. **Invalid session name characters:** SessionNamePrompt validates against `^[a-zA-Z0-9_-]+$`. Show inline error for invalid characters. This matches the backend's validSessionName regex (terminal.go:171) to prevent 400 errors.

7. **Empty session name:** Submit button is disabled when input is empty or whitespace-only.

8. **Closing active tab:** When the active tab is closed, select the tab to its left (index - 1). If closing the first tab, select the new first tab. Never close the last remaining tab.

9. **Closing tab while search is open:** If the closed tab was active and search is open, clear searchTerm and call clearSearch on the newly active tab, then re-run the current search on it.

10. **Tab switch while search is open:** A useEffect watches activeTabId + searchTerm: when switching tabs with search open and a non-empty term, re-run search on the new active instance.

11. **Cmd+F when TerminalView not visible:** The keydown listener is registered in useEffect and cleaned up on unmount, so this is handled automatically.

12. **Search on empty term:** When searchTerm is cleared, call clearSearch on the active instance to remove highlight decorations.

13. **Race condition with ref callbacks:** Search handlers use optional chaining on `instanceRefs.current.get(activeTabId)?.search(...)` to handle the case where the ref isn't available yet.

14. **Full-height toggle with body scroll:** useEffect sets `document.body.style.overflow = "hidden"` when full-height is active, restores on cleanup.

15. **Connection state updates:** handleConnectionStateChange uses functional setState `setTabs(prev => prev.map(...))` to avoid stale closures.

16. **Session prompt dismissed with Escape:** Closes the modal, no tab created, no side effects.

