### `services/auth/src/lib/logger.ts`
Structured JSON logger with secret redaction. Structure:

```typescript
// Log levels
type LogLevel = "debug" | "info" | "warn" | "error";

// Numeric priority for level filtering
const LEVEL_PRIORITY = { debug: 0, info: 1, warn: 2, error: 3 };

// Fields that must NEVER appear in log output
const REDACTED_FIELDS = new Set([
  "token", "secret", "password", "authorization",
  "cookie", "jwt", "access_token", "refresh_token",
  "client_secret", "better_auth_secret",
]);

// Recursively redact sensitive fields from objects
function redact(obj: Record<string, unknown>): Record<string, unknown>;

// Logger class
class Logger {
  private level: LogLevel;

  constructor(level?: LogLevel);  // defaults to env.LOG_LEVEL

  debug(msg: string, data?: Record<string, unknown>): void;
  info(msg: string, data?: Record<string, unknown>): void;
  warn(msg: string, data?: Record<string, unknown>): void;
  error(msg: string, data?: Record<string, unknown>): void;

  // Output: JSON line to stdout
  // Format: {"level":"info","msg":"...","ts":"ISO8601",...redacted_data}
  // Errors go to stderr
}

// Singleton export
export const logger: Logger;
export { Logger, LogLevel };
```

Key design notes:
- Outputs one JSON object per line (structured logging, compatible with log aggregators)
- `redact()` does a shallow clone of the object, replacing values of redacted keys with `"[REDACTED]"`. Handles nested objects one level deep (sufficient for log payloads — no deep recursion needed).
- `ts` field uses `new Date().toISOString()` for UTC timestamps
- `error` level writes to stderr, all others to stdout
- No colors, no fancy formatting — this is a production server logger

### `services/auth/src/lib/metrics.ts`
Prometheus counter registry. Structure:

```typescript
// Simple counter implementation (no external dependency)
class Counter {
  private name: string;
  private help: string;
  private value: number = 0;

  constructor(name: string, help: string);
  inc(): void;
  get(): number;
  toPrometheus(): string;  // "# HELP ...\n# TYPE ... counter\n<name> <value>"
}

// Registry of all auth service metrics
export const metrics = {
  signInAttempts: new Counter(
    "auth_sign_in_attempts_total",
    "Total number of sign-in attempts"
  ),
  tokenIssued: new Counter(
    "auth_token_issued_total",
    "Total number of JWT tokens issued"
  ),
  sessionCreated: new Counter(
    "auth_session_created_total",
    "Total number of sessions created"
  ),
  rateLimitTriggered: new Counter(
    "auth_rate_limit_triggered_total",
    "Total number of rate limit rejections"
  ),
  jwksRotation: new Counter(
    "auth_jwks_rotation_total",
    "Total number of JWKS key rotations"
  ),
};

// Render all metrics in Prometheus text exposition format
export function renderMetrics(): string;
```

Key design notes:
- No external Prometheus client library — five simple counters, a full library is overkill
- Thread-safe by default in Node.js (single-threaded event loop)
- Follows Prometheus naming conventions: `snake_case`, `_total` suffix for counters
- `renderMetrics()` concatenates all counter outputs with blank line separators
- Counters are monotonically increasing (never reset except on process restart)

