## Summary

Create a thin React wrapper around CodeMirror 6 that provides a declarative component API for embedding a code editor. This component will be used by both the File Explorer (read-only syntax-highlighted viewing) and the File Editor (full editing with Cmd+S save, Cmd+F search, dirty tracking). It handles EditorView lifecycle, language switching via compartments, and dynamic resizing via ResizeObserver.

## Technical Approach

**Pattern:** Follow the TerminalPanel xterm.js integration pattern — create the EditorView in a useEffect with ref-based DOM attachment, full cleanup on unmount, and debounced ResizeObserver for dynamic sizing. Use refs for all CM6 instances (EditorView, Compartment) to avoid stale closures.

**Language switching:** Use a CM6 Compartment for the language extension. When the \`language\` prop changes, reconfigure the compartment via \`view.dispatch({ effects: languageCompartment.reconfigure(...) })\` rather than destroying/recreating the entire editor. This preserves cursor position, undo history, and scroll state.

**Value sync:** Use EditorView.updateListener to detect document changes and call \`onChange\`. For external value changes (e.g., loading a new file), compare against current doc content and use \`view.dispatch({ changes: { from: 0, to: doc.length, insert: newValue } })\` only when the value actually differs (avoiding cursor-resetting loops).

**No forwardRef/useImperativeHandle:** Following the codebase convention of props-and-callbacks only. Search is handled by CM6's built-in Cmd+F/Ctrl+F keybinding (included via \`searchKeymap\`), so the parent doesn't need to trigger it programmatically. If a parent needs to open search, it can pass a \`searchOpen\` boolean prop that triggers \`openSearchPanel(view)\` via a useEffect.

**Stale closure handling:** Following the LogViewer pattern — store onChange in a ref and sync it via a dedicated useEffect: \`useEffect(() => { onChangeRef.current = onChange }, [onChange])\`. This prevents stale closures in the EditorView.updateListener callback.

**ResizeObserver:** Include a debounced ResizeObserver (matching TerminalPanel pattern) that calls \`view.requestMeasure()\` on container resize. CM6 handles internal layout but needs explicit notification when the parent container resizes (panel drag, window resize).

**Theme:** The editor appears inline in the app's light theme context, not in a terminal context. All theme overrides use design system light tokens (--bg-card, --text-primary, --font-family-mono). Dark mode support uses the existing useTheme/CSS variable system — CM6 base theme maps to CSS custom properties so it adapts automatically.

**Language packs:** Start with only the languages agents actually edit in this codebase: lang-go, lang-json, lang-yaml, lang-markdown. Additional packs (lang-javascript, lang-python, lang-css, lang-html) can be added later on demand without changing the component API.

