## Edge Cases & Error Handling

1. **Pre-migration users who still have \`loom-active-workspace\` in localStorage:** The V6→V7 migration handles this — it reads the old key, resolves the name to UUID, stores the UUID in \`loom:last-workspace-id\`, and removes the old key. After this fix, the old key will not be re-created. Expected behavior: the migration runs once and the old key stays deleted permanently.

2. **Post-fix users on fresh install (no \`loom-active-workspace\` key ever):** No issue. \`setLastWorkspaceId(workspaceId)\` writes to the canonical key. The old key never appears.

